Aeron 1.53.1 C media driver: a failed setup-eliciting status message no longer wedges the session.

aeron_data_packet_dispatcher_elicit_setup_from_source marks the session PENDING_SETUP_FRAME, sends the status
message that asks the source for a setup frame and, when that send fails (EPERM from a local firewall rule,
ENETUNREACH or EHOSTUNREACH while inbound traffic has already recovered), returned -1 before
aeron_driver_receiver_add_pending_setup. With no pending setup there is no timer to clear the state, every later
frame of that session is ignored (on_data elicits only from the initial state) and a source that already had a
connection sends setup frames only when asked: no image forms until a process restarts.

The Java driver always adds the pending setup (DataPacketDispatcher.elicitSetupMessageFromSource; its
ReceiveChannelEndpoint.sendTo logs a send error and returns). This patch does the same: the failed send is logged
as the receiver logs its other send errors (distinct error log and the errors counter) and the pending setup is
still registered, so after the pending-setup timeout the session is back in the initial state and the next frame
elicits a setup again.

Applied by cmake/VerifiedDependencies.cmake to the tree extracted from the tarball dependencies.lock pins; its
sha256 is pinned there too (aeron_patches). Test: tests/aeron-driver (aeron_driver.elicit_setup_retry).

--- a/aeron-driver/src/main/c/aeron_data_packet_dispatcher.c
+++ b/aeron-driver/src/main/c/aeron_data_packet_dispatcher.c
@@ -641,8 +641,14 @@
         endpoint, destination, control_addr, stream_id, session_id, 0, 0, 0,
         AERON_STATUS_MESSAGE_HEADER_SEND_SETUP_FLAG) < 0)
     {
-        AERON_APPEND_ERR("%s", "");
-        return -1;
+        /*
+         * Log the failed send as the receiver logs its other send errors and still register the pending setup, as the
+         * Java driver does (ReceiveChannelEndpoint.sendTo logs and returns, DataPacketDispatcher then adds the pending
+         * setup message). Returning here left the session in PENDING_SETUP_FRAME with no pending setup to time it
+         * out, so no later frame of that session could elicit a setup again and the image never formed.
+         */
+        AERON_APPEND_ERR("%s", "receiver send setup eliciting SM");
+        aeron_driver_receiver_log_error(dispatcher->receiver);
     }
 
     if (aeron_driver_receiver_add_pending_setup(
